def ReplaceGraphicStyleFromImage(_iColorwayIndex : int, _graphicstyleIndex : int, _imagePath : str, _anchor : int, _width : float, _height : float) -> bool
"""
@ingroup UTILITY_API
@brief Replace the graphic style image for ONE colorway with an explicit display size.
If the style is currently linked (shared) across colorways it is automatically
unlinked for the target colorway first, so other colorways are NOT affected.
The graphic is resized to exactly (_width x _height) mm regardless of anchor choice.

@param _iColorwayIndex: index of the colorway to target
@param _graphicstyleIndex: index within that colorway's graphic style list
@param _imagePath: path to the new image file
@param _anchor: anchor point to hold fixed. Accepts plain integers or Marvelous::CloApiAnchorPoint enum values:
0=Center  1=Up  2=RightUp  3=Right  4=RightDown
5=Down  6=LeftDown  7=Left  8=LeftUp
@param _width:  target display width  in mm
@param _height: target display height in mm
@return true if successful, false if any index is out of range or the style is not applied in the target colorway

@example Linked graphic — replace only colorway 0, colorway 1 unchanged:

BEFORE (both linked to the same style)
Colorway 0 --+
+--> [ old_logo ]
Colorway 1 --+

AFTER  ReplaceGraphicStyleFromImage(0, idx, "new_logo", CLOAPI_ANCHOR_LEFT_UP, 60, 30)
Colorway 0 ------> [ new_logo 60x30mm ]  (auto-unlinked, top-left pinned)
Colorway 1 ------> [ old_logo ]  (untouched)

@example Already-unlinked graphic — replacement proceeds normally:

Colorway 0 ------> [ logo_A ]      Colorway 0 ------> [ new_logo 60x30mm ]
Colorway 1 ------> [ logo_B ]  --> Colorway 1 ------> [ logo_B ]  (untouched)

"""

```

